# Monorepo Workflow

## Package boundaries

- Editor features → `packages/{excalidraw,element,common,math,utils}`
- Runnable app → `excalidraw-app/` (start with `yarn start` → http://localhost:3001)
- Examples/docs → `examples/`, `dev-docs/` (require `yarn build:packages` first)
- Dev server resolves `@excalidraw/*` from **source** — do not run `build:packages` for normal editor work

## Canonical commands (repo root)

| Goal | Command |
|------|---------|
| Typecheck | `yarn test:typecheck` |
| Focused tests | `yarn test:app --watch=false <path>` |
| Update snapshots | `yarn test:update` (review diffs deliberately) |
| Lint | `yarn test:code` |
| Auto-fix | `yarn fix` |
| Branch from ticket | `./scripts/br.sh <ec-n> <slug>` |

Prefer `yarn test:typecheck` as the first verification after type-union changes. Use focused tests, not the full suite, unless the user asks.

## Known gotchas — do not "fix" unless asked

- `actionStyles.test.tsx`: 16 prettier warnings make `yarn test:code` exit non-zero; Vitest worker IPC can flake on this file
- vite-plugin-checker may show false-positive TS errors in `MermaidToExcalidraw.test.tsx`; authoritative check is `yarn test:typecheck`
- Optional backends (collab WS, AI) are **not** required for core drawing

## Demo safety

- Never push seeded demo bugs (`seed-demo-bug` skill)
- Never commit directly to `master` unless explicitly asked
- Use `demo-reset` / `./scripts/demo-reset.sh` to return to pristine baseline
